arly in individuals with bipolar disorder or predisposition. Clinical guidance mandates immediate discontinuation upon emergence of manic symptoms [Data: Relationships (14524); Entities (17520)]. This adverse reaction is a well-known class effect among antidepressants but underscores the necessity of thorough psychiatric screening before initiating SSRI therapy.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"抗精神病药物 commonly cause excessive sedation, especially with co-ingestants\",\n            \"explanation\": \"抗精神病药物 (antipsychotics) are frequently associated with 过度镇静 (excessive sedation), a dose-dependent and pharmacologically predictable adverse effect. This risk is amplified when antipsychotics are combined with other CNS depressants such as alcohol, leading to potentially dangerous levels of central suppression [Data: Relationships (12008)]. The interaction exemplifies pharmacodynamic synergy that can compromise patient safety, particularly in outpatient or polysubstance-use contexts.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"色氨酸 interacts with MAO inhibitors like 苯乙肼, posing theoretical serotonergic risks\",\n            \"explanation\": \"色氨酸 (tryptophan), an amino acid precursor to serotonin, interacts with monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs) such as 苯乙肼 (phenelzine). Although the provided evidence focuses on metabolic and hypoglycemic interactions, the combination of serotonergic agents with MAOIs is historically linked to serotonin syndrome—a life-threatening condition [Data: Relationships (49418)]. While the excerpt does not explicitly mention serotonin toxicity, the known pharmacology of these agents warrants caution regarding this high-severity interaction.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"噻吗咯尔 interferes with metabolism of multiple CNS-active drugs\",\n            \"explanation\": \"噻吗咯尔 (timolol), a non-selective beta-blocker, competitively inhibits the metabolism of several centrally acting drugs, including 盐酸